# Web-facing hardening for the Purchase Order app.
#
# Everything the browser legitimately needs is a .php page, a css/js/font/image
# asset under system/, or an uploaded avatar. Nothing else in this tree should
# ever be retrievable over HTTP — most importantly system/.env, which holds the
# live HRMIS database password and the QR signing key in plaintext.

# No directory listings anywhere. Without this, /vb/, /tools/, /system/uploads/
# and /system/database/ all enumerate their contents to anonymous visitors.
Options -Indexes

# Dotfiles (.env, .git*, .htpasswd …) and developer material: schema dumps,
# docs, legacy sources, editor leftovers. Denied by name so a new file of a
# known-sensitive type is covered the moment it lands, not when someone
# remembers to add a rule.
<FilesMatch "^\.|\.(env|sql|md|bak|orig|save|swp|log|rpt|vb|vbproj|sln|resx|config)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>
